// expect: refused
// why: a pattern binds every field of a variant's payload or none of them, never some
// spec:  §enum-match-arity-4jq7wnm
// from: the mutation sweep, where `case C(p, q)` on a one-field variant was a family nothing reported
//
// **Not a partial binding.** Omitting the parentheses ignores the whole payload and is ordinary —
// `case Rect:` is in the spec beside this — so the tempting reading of `case Rect(w)` is "bind the
// first field and ignore the rest". It is not: a name in the wrong position would be a different
// field with no diagnostic, which is the failure a fixed arity exists to prevent.
//
// The reference reports it at the `case` keyword and says how many names against how many fields.
// wacc said nothing at all until 2026-08-17, in either direction: `case C(p, q)` on a one-field
// variant bound `q` to nothing, and the whole category was missed.

enum Shape {
  Point,
  Rect(f64 w, f64 h),
}

export f64 area(Shape s) {
  match (s) {
    case Rect(w): { return w; }
    else: { return 0.0; }
  }
}
